🧪 4. Simulating Verilog Code

1. Tools: Use simulators like ModelSim (QuestaSim), Icarus Verilog (free), or Verilator.

2. Testbench: Stimulate the design and check outputs.

Simple Testbench:

module tb;
reg a, b;
wire y;

and_gate uut (a, b, y); // Instantiate design under test (DUT)

initial begin
$monitor("a=%b, b=%b, y=%b", a, b, y);
a = 0; b = 0; #10;
a = 0; b = 1; #10;
a = 1; b = 0; #10;
a = 1; b = 1; #10;
$finish;
end
endmodule

Compile and run using Icarus Verilog (free simulator):

iverilog -o and_gate_tb and_gate.v and_gate_tb.v
vvp and_gate_tb

