How to get started:
• Write an FSM for start bit, data bits, stop bit
• Use a counter to generate baud tick
• Transmit a byte, capture waveforms
• Add parity as an extension
• Build a loopback testbench

5. Build a round robin arbiter
Arbiters appear inside buses, NoCs, caches and many SoCs.

What you learn:
• Priority rotation
• Fairness logic
• Clean FSMs
• Scalable design

