Why these tiny projects matter
Small RTL designs teach you real engineering intuition. They force you to:
• Write clean, synthesizable code
• Think in cycles instead of lines
• Debug using waveforms
• Separate datapath and control
• Understand protocols and timing
• Build reusable modules
